{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2572 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "6dcd08012bdff1bce94847212c60b27ce958949234e9d2479536e208c6a0e47f" :edb/db-before-t 2571 :edb/db-after-t 2572 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535884 50 #inst "2026-10-09T09:52:11.199Z" 13194139535884 true] [17592186171786 1100 "Which of the following regions are connected?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/ef9e1dfd559c1e8818f14e100e07ab36ca167a4bd2ddf970bf3f5ef325103d64.png)" 13194139535884 true] [17592186171786 1100 "Which of the following regions are connected?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3357/Source/Images/8bc6eee716b3c35ded2c54628da21226.png)" 13194139535884 false] [17592186171786 1145 "A region $D$ is connected if every pair of points in $D$ can be joined by a smooth curve or a path in $D$.\n\nAmong the given options, only regions I, II, and III satisfy this definition.\n\nRegion IV does not satisfy this definition. Note that if we take two points $P$ and $Q$, as shown below, there is no path lying entirely within the region that connects them.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3357/Source/Images/4c9ec6c4f35d8902525483f7a86d70af.png)" 13194139535884 false] [17592186171786 1145 "A region $D$ is connected if every pair of points in $D$ can be joined by a smooth curve or a path in $D.$\n\nAmong the given options, only regions I, II, and III satisfy this definition.\n\nRegion IV does not satisfy this definition. Note that if we take two points $P$ and $Q$, as shown below, there is no path lying entirely within the region that connects them.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/d4d61cf87f2c62c5cf4727384d6dfcc05cada6b23025dd6dd674130eaf64dd45.png)" 13194139535884 true] [17592186171787 1100 "Which of the regions shown below are simply connected?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/b8e630b749cbfee41d73a620ffd284f3216bb8a43affdc26543f1eb57e4613c5.png)" 13194139535884 true] [17592186171787 1100 "Which of the regions shown below are simply connected?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3357/Source/Images/1164dfedfd68fecee2af1031295ffb86.png)" 13194139535884 false] [17592186171787 1145 "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the regions: \n\n- Region I is not simply connected. Instead, this is a connected region that contains a hole.\n\n- Region II is simply connected. This is a connected region that does not contain holes.\n\n- Region III is not simply connected. Instead, this is a region that consists of two pieces (it's not connected).\n\n- Region IV is simply connected. This is a connected region that does not contain holes.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and IV only.\"" 13194139535884 true] [17592186171787 1145 "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3357/Source/Images/06bab6e6cec4b75e4a1363b4dbc20310.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D$. In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3357/Source/Images/42d126c7bd2ac311262b659d2596dc37.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the regions:\n\n- Region I is not simply connected. Instead, this is a connected region that contains a hole.\n- Region II is simply connected. This is a connected region that does not contain holes.\n- Region III is not simply connected. Instead, this is a region that consists of two pieces (it's not connected).\n- Region IV is simply connected. This is a connected region that does not contain holes.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and IV only.\"" 13194139535884 false] [17592186171829 1100 "Which of the following regions are simply connected?\n\n- $\\{(x,y) \\in \\mathbb R^2 \\: | \\: y-x\\geq 0\\}$\n\n- $\\{(x,y) \\in \\mathbb R^2 \\: | \\: (x,y)\\neq (0,0)\\}$\n\n- $\\{(x,y)\\in \\mathbb R^2 \\: | \\: x^2+y^2> 4\\}$" 13194139535884 true] [17592186171829 1100 "Which of the following regions are simply connected?\n\n1. $\\{(x,y) \\in \\mathbb R^2 \\: \\mid \\: y-x\\geq 0\\}$\n2. $\\{(x,y) \\in \\mathbb R^2 \\: \\mid \\: (x,y)\\neq (0,0)\\}$\n3. $\\{(x,y)\\in \\mathbb R^2 \\: \\mid \\: x^2+y^2> 4\\}$" 13194139535884 false] [17592186171829 1145 "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nLet's now examine our regions in turn.\n\n- Region I is simply connected. Indeed, it is the half-plane $y \\geq x.$ So, it's a plane region without holes.\n\n- Region II is *not*  simply connected since it's a plane region with a hole at $(0,0).$\n\n- Region III is *not* simply connected since it's a plane region with a hole. In this case, the hole contains all points on the disc $x^2+y^2 \\leq 4$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139535884 true] [17592186171829 1145 "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3357/Source/Images/998c3fae4e98a4fcb65db22d9a3b178a.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D$. In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3357/Source/Images/06500334cbe214f995d2491dc71265a1.png)\n\nLet's now examine our regions in turn.\n\n- Region I is simply connected. Indeed, it is the half-plane $y \\geq x$. So, it's a plane region without holes.\n- Region II is *not* simply connected since it's a plane region with a hole at $(0,0)$.\n- Region III is *not* simply connected since it's a plane region with a hole. In this case, the hole contains all points on the disc $x^2+y^2 \\leq 4$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139535884 false] [17592186171980 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372461 13194139535884 true] [17592186171980 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372510 13194139535884 true] [17592186171980 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372517 13194139535884 true] [17592186171981